# chacha20 — RFC 8439 ChaCha20.
#
# Three modules, smallest first. `chacha20_qr` is one quarter round and
# exists because RFC 8439 §2.1.1 is a test vector for it. `chacha20_core`
# is the block function of §2.3 — four quarter rounds a cycle, twenty
# rounds, 22 cycles a block. `chacha20` is the encryption of §2.4: the
# keystream exclusive-ored with a 32-bit stream, the counter advanced per
# block, and a stop when the counter would run out. `top` names that one.
#
# There is no Poly1305 here, so nothing in this package authenticates
# anything. `ip/crypto/chacha20/README.md` §6 is about that, and §4 and
# §5 are about what the constant-time claim covers and what it does not.
name chacha20
version 1.0.0
license MIT
description "RFC 8439 ChaCha20: the quarter round, the block function at one round per cycle, and the stream cipher over a 32-bit ready/valid stream"

top chacha20
target ice40
target ecp5

source rtl/chacha20_qr.v
source rtl/chacha20_core.v
source rtl/chacha20.v

port clk in
port rst_n in
port start in
port key in 256
port nonce in 96
port counter in 32
port in_data in 32
port in_valid in
port in_ready out
port out_data out 32
port out_valid out
port active out
port exhausted out
